Phase 8h: Replace caller rewriting with native OpenTK binding interception
  Depends on 8g.
  Authority: [Rendering.OpenTKBindingInterception.Proposal.md](Rendering.OpenTKBindingInterception.Proposal.md),
    the approved RHI proposal/contracts, and retained resource/binding/publication authority.
  Outcome: supported OpenTK native dispatch reaches one observational interception authority independent
    of caller assembly; backend-owned dispatch and manager/cache publication remain singular.

  ☑ Establish the complete selected-operation/native-signature inventory from EngineStateCallMap,
    EngineMetadataCallAdapters/MetadataAdapterCatalog and existing backend observation owners. Cover both
    legacy OpenGL.GL and OpenGL4.GL tables and supported Core/Ext/Arb entrypoints. Preserve exclusions for
    other auxiliary owners and legacy compatibility features. Define coverage as calls through those tables,
    not unrelated graphics libraries or independently cached driver pointers. Distinguish queries/content
    effects requiring observation from operations with no represented state/lifetime contract.
  ☑ Replace handwritten callback boilerplate with a narrowly scoped source generator. Declare selected
    native entrypoints on handwritten post-call observer methods using attributes; resolve entrypoint names
    against native signatures derived from the exact compiler-referenced OpenTK.Graphics assembly and
    compiler-check observer parameter/return-value
    mappings. Diagnose unknown entrypoints, incompatible signatures and duplicate registrations at build time.
    Use compiler-resolved symbols for project methods rather than unchecked method-name strings.
    Read binding-table name initialization and calli signatures at build time without loading OpenTK or
    executing static constructors. Remove the maintained NativeSignatures.txt input. Diagnose unsupported
    layouts and conflicting native ABIs; managed convenience overloads must not determine native signatures.
  ☑ Generate ABI-correct callback delegates/thunks, registration and saved-original dispatch plumbing from
    the same declarations. Preserve native widths, calling conventions, return values and output pointers;
    keep reflection, dynamic invocation and per-call delegate allocation out of generated dispatch.
    Keep generated plumbing separate from handwritten domain-specific cache/publication effects.
  ☑ Use post-call observation exclusively: invoke the original native operation once with unchanged
    arguments, then invoke its observer with the arguments and any native result. Generate observer exception
    containment and an observation-enabled check after native dispatch. Do not generate preparation hooks, before/after
    hook pairs or an observer-controlled native invocation. Never retry the native operation after observer
    failure, and preserve its return/output values even when observation fails.
  ☑ Migrate existing callbacks, including BindTexture, BindVertexArray, BindTransformFeedback and BlendFunci,
    to post-call observers in complete operation-family units. Reassess current Begin/Complete dependencies:
    use existing cached prior facts where valid, account for reentrant changes and output-buffer mutation,
    and never assume cached pre-call facts remain valid across nested calls. Keep conflict interruption and
    targeted failure recovery within existing cache/manager authority, executed after native dispatch.
    Remove superseded handwritten callback factories/catalog entries and duplicate dispatch boilerplate;
    do not retain parallel routes or introduce migration shims.
  ☑ Simplify cache delivery: put attributes on cache-owned observation methods and let ABI-identical aliases
    share one method. Generate direct calls rather than installation-owned forwarding observers. Normalize
    bound/named effects within each domain; remove immediate Begin/Complete dispatch receipts when they
    add no lifetime or failure contract. Keep manager publication and reentrant acquisition recovery intact.
    All observation families use single post-call operations: buffer binding/storage/texture association,
    VAO selection/configuration, program selection/metadata, renderbuffer storage, texture metadata and
    transform-feedback activity. Remove all 169 immediate pairs, ten receipt types and the nested
    buffer-binding/VAO receipt. Migrate the five shared backend callers to synchronous execution owners
    that preserve actual native work and failure cleanup; update direct receipt-based tests to exercise
    real acquisition, interruption, context ownership and controlled-operation failure.
    Generate consumed OpenGLDriverCalls overloads from exact compiler-selected OpenTK overloads, with no
    handwritten bypass inventory. Test indexed overload resolution and original-pointer execution.
  ☑ Qualify the generator with compilation/diagnostic tests and representative generated native-call tests.
    Cover void/non-void signatures where selected, pointer/output arguments, aliases and both OpenTK tables;
    prove original dispatch precedes observation, observer failure preserves native results, and callback
    disabled observers are skipped while native dispatch and results remain intact. Verify generated coverage matches every selected inventory entry.
  ☑ Implement validated installation beneath the OpenGL backend. Identify supported binding layouts and
    entrypoints without treating experimental numeric slot indices as stable API names. Use exact native
    widths/calling conventions and callback lifetimes; retain true original pointers privately. No OpenTK
    type/pointer or translation helper may leak into portable RHI APIs, wrappers or manager services.
  ☑ Integrate installation with startup and every supported LoadBindings path for both tables. Handle
    already-loaded bindings, repeated installation, replacement arrays and loader failure without recording
    our callbacks as original driver addresses. Define safe loader/execution coordination and teardown;
    disable observation and atomically restore only entries still owned by this installation without waiting
    for executing calls. Retain delegates/original pointers so already-fetched callbacks remain safe; an
    admitted observer may finish. Coordinate cache/resource destruction through the existing lifecycle.
    Remove per-call enter/exit counters and deferred-uninstall machinery.
  ☑ Bind observation to originating physical context/thread and registered lifetime using existing authority.
    Shared loader tables must not imply shared state knowledge. Resolve original dispatch pointers for the
    applicable loader/context lifetime; preserve foreign-context completion and retirement behavior.
  ☑ Implement always-forward observation: an external call executes its original native operation exactly
    once with unchanged arguments, return values, output buffers and native errors. No equality suppression,
    managed admission rejection, native-call cancellation, deferred execution or retry on this route.
    Run observers only after native dispatch and contain reconciliation faults without repeating it.
    No observer exception escapes the callback or is deferred back to the external caller.
  ☑ Replace rejection-style external observer guards with non-vetoing bookkeeping. Cover
    RequireMutableFramebufferConfiguration, RequireOutsideEngineBoundary/unsupported-boundary mutation,
    RequireResourceOperationAvailable and manager OperationInProgress/CompletionInProgress checks wherever
    they currently block exact forwarding. Native mutations still reach GL; reflect conflicting effects
    through existing operation interruption, availability and certificate invalidation. Managed RHI API
    validation remains separate. Do not hide the old rejection behind catch-and-return that skips GL.
  ☑ Extract/reuse canonical effect logic so callbacks do not invoke an exact adapter that dispatches again.
    Preserve argument-derived/default/derived propagation completed in 8g, target/unit/indexed/object-local
    aliases and per-field masks. Observation failure withdraws only uncertain affected knowledge; recipient
    notification failure cannot undo an already committed canonical publication. No second state cache,
    resource registry, callback-owned resource lifetime or requested/actual metadata mirror.
  ☑ Route backend-owned native execution through its saved original dispatch boundary, preserving existing
    RHI admission, eligible suppression, original-context validation and exactly-once manager publication.
    Avoid broad suppression flags hiding nested external calls. Qualify recursion, reentry, extension aliases
    and any driver-internal dispatch so one logical external effect is not published twice.
  ☑ Complete remaining program/pipeline selector propagation and transform-feedback activity acceptance.
    Cover UseProgram/UseProgramObject, BindProgramPipeline, ActiveShaderProgram/EXT active-program variants,
    BindTransformFeedback and Begin/End/Pause/ResumeTransformFeedback where supported. Distinguish current
    program, pipeline selection, active uniform destination and executable stage facts. Establish accepted,
    rejected and uncertain effects without universal queries; remove redundant active-state recapture when
    observed history proves the fact. Installed-engine nonuse does not prove wider OpenTK calls impossible.
  ☑ Finish the remaining resource-configuration/selector forget-and-query inventory under the new route.
    Account explicitly for native allocation/outcome uncertainty, initial facts, deletion-in-use and
    unrepresented schemas. Preserve the approved narrow query policy, native errors and existing empty
    VAO/sampler/query schemas; do not query merely to verify supplied facts or expand metadata without need.
  ☑ Migrate each full operation family with its callers/tests in one unit. Remove its EngineStateTargets,
    EngineGenericStateTargets, EngineStateSwitchingHook and EngineRenderApiStatePatches obligations as they
    become obsolete; remove exact native adapter/dispatcher routes superseded by callbacks. Retain broader
    engine shader/render integration hooks only where their separate semantic purpose still applies.
    Final closure removes obsolete caller scanning/maps, generic closure caches and forwarding modules;
    never leave old and new observers simultaneously active or introduce intermediate migration shims.
  ☑ Qualify direct, delegate, generic value-type and late-loaded/dynamically generated OpenTK callers in
    both tables, including warm/already-compiled paths, with native-state and output-data oracles. Verify
    backend bypass, unchanged rejected-command errors, original arguments/return/output values, exactly-once
    dispatch/publication and alias effects. The isolated feasibility probe is evidence, not production proof.
  ☑ Inject faults throughout post-call observation and its recovery; prove native calls executed once and uncertain
    facts are withdrawn without stale guesses, unrelated purges or caller exceptions. Cover reentry,
    immutable/boundary conflicts, interrupted manager operations and failed recipient notifications.
    Exercise initial/reloaded tables, concurrent loader/dispatch policy, physical context changes, retirement,
    callbacks in flight and teardown; no swallowed-failure native-call cancellation is acceptable.
  ☑ Run delegated canonical Debug/ordinary Release builds and focused regressions on the completed family
    replacement. Perform second review and independent audit; reconcile proposal/contracts, inventory/API
    coverage, migration receipts, parent-plan references and permanent current-state documentation. Keep
    installed-game startup/live evidence and broader hardware limitations explicit; no benchmark or timing gate.
  ☑ Completion: the supported OpenTK tables have one qualified always-forward observation path, managed RHI
    execution bypasses duplicate observation, superseded caller rewriting is removed, and accepted effects
    propagate through the existing cache/manager without avoidable recapture or external-call vetoes.

  Implementation checkpoint: OpenGLInterceptionGenerator derives native signatures and consumed
    OpenGLDriverCalls overloads from the compiler's OpenTK.Graphics PE reference. Generated callbacks
    directly invoke cache-owned observations; identical aliases share handlers. There are 308 selected
    native entrypoints; three former read-routing observers had no represented effect and are omitted.
    All 169 immediate receipt pairs, ten receipt types, the nested buffer-binding/VAO receipt and unused
    native observation guard factory are removed. Production and test source scans find zero old factory
    references. Controlled vertex configuration and program assignment keep actual execution and cleanup
    inside backend owners; the cache exposes observation and knowledge updates.
    Completion qualification: canonical Debug and ordinary Release builds pass with shader targets
    enabled and no JIT overrides. The final combined selection passes 662/662 per configuration,
    zero skips (artifacts/phase8h/closure7-*, exact filter closure7-filter.txt). Unchanged generator
    sources retain 18/18 tests in both configurations. Second source review and the separate
    audit-stage-completion contract audit pass; no required 8h item remains open.
    Broad diagnostic execution and archived HEAD comparison identified 477 inherited failures and
    sequence-dependent integration observations. All initially unmatched classes pass the final
    combined selection, but full-suite ordering/output acceptance remains explicitly in Phase 9.
    No package, installed-game startup, live appearance or wider hardware qualification is claimed.
