Phase 8h.1: Correct effect classification and simplify native observation delivery
  Depends on 8h's implemented native dispatch boundary; precedes 8i's metadata lifecycle redesign.
  Authority: [Rendering.OpenTKBindingInterception.Proposal.md](Rendering.OpenTKBindingInterception.Proposal.md),
    [Rendering.GpuCommands.Contracts.md](Rendering.GpuCommands.Contracts.md), existing cache/manager
    publication authority and [Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.ApiCoverage.md](Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.ApiCoverage.md).
  Outcome: small handwritten effect handlers use shared generated delivery/recovery plumbing; only
    represented effects interrupt or publish metadata, and ordinary startup does not rely on exceptions.
  Follow-up finding: 8h's focused receipts do not cover the newly identified LineWidth context-rule gap.
    Correct that behavior here; preserve the historical receipts without treating them as proof of this fix.

  ☑ Review native effect classification independently of argument validity. Distinguish a known change,
    proven rejection and uncertain outcome using existing context/profile/capability and resource facts.
    Correct ObserveLineWidth: a positive finite width is not sufficient evidence of acceptance;
    widths above one are rejected in a forward-compatible context. Use the already captured
    IsForwardCompatibleContext fact, preserve prior line-width knowledge after proven rejection and
    retain the caller's native error. Review equivalent state/profile-dependent omissions in other
    setters, including ObservePatchParameteri. Add no universal GetError, Is* or verification queries,
    requested/actual mirror or native-call veto. Consult [OpenGL 4.6 core appendix E.2.1](https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL/specs/gl/glspec46.core.pdf)
    and the registry definitions controlling each selected operation.
  ☑ Design and implement generated common observation plumbing for simple setters, explicitly covering
    ObserveLogicOp, ObserveDepthMask, ObserveLineWidth and ObservePatchParameteri. Move repeated
    context selection/capture, affected-field withdrawal, post-call delivery and contained targeted
    failure recovery into one compiler-checked path using explicit Withdraw method references.
    Keep affected-field selection in handwritten cache methods receiving the cache and native arguments;
    do not mirror knowledge categories on InterceptOpenGLAttribute or inside the generator.
    Keep GL acceptance/conversion semantics and state assignments in focused handwritten domain code;
    do not build a generic event bus, transaction framework or semantic interpreter in the generator.
    Preserve original-context/lifetime checks and recovery that withdraws only affected uncertain facts.
    The generator's existing outer catch alone is insufficient to replace handler-local recovery.
    Remove redundant casts, unused argument locals, constant accepted flags and duplicate context capture
    where the resulting contract makes them unnecessary. Keep one observation/publication authority.
  ☑ Reassess which native entrypoints need metadata observation. Remove the sampler/image-unit
    metadata routes for ObserveUniform1uiEXT and ObserveUniform1uivEXT: unsigned numeric uniform
    setters cannot assign sampler/image units, and ordinary numeric uniform contents have no represented
    canonical metadata effect. Audit related scalar/vector/named/extension spellings for the same issue.
    Keep signed Uniform1i/Uniform1iv, named equivalents and opaque-handle assignments observed where
    they affect represented units or representation availability. Consult OpenGL 4.6 core section 7.6
    and [EXT_gpu_shader4 uniform-loading semantics](https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL/extensions/EXT/EXT_gpu_shader4.txt).
    Unobserved content-only calls still execute natively unchanged. Reconcile selected-symbol inventory, ABI/catalog generation, API
    dispositions and tests; preserve semantic coverage rather than an arbitrary callback count.
  ☑ Reorder ObserveProgramMetadata so represented-effect classification precedes
    InterruptNativeResourceOperation, InterruptNativeMetadataCompletion, BeginRefresh and publication.
    An ordinary numeric uniform write or ignored location must not interrupt an otherwise valid
    acquisition/publication, withdraw unrelated facts, advance metadata revisions or trigger avoidable
    descriptor queries. Use established selector/interface facts; retain interruption and targeted
    recovery for actual represented unit/block/executable mutations, including reentrant callbacks.
    Review equivalent relevance-after-interruption ordering throughout native observation families.
  ☑ Replace exception-based handling of expected initialization absence in
    OpenGLObservationContext.CurrentCache with an explicit query-free TryGet-style result or equivalent
    direct control flow. Separate originating-context selection from full capability availability:
    capability-independent effects such as DepthMask and LogicOp should not require unrelated cached
    limits. Capability-dependent handlers must classify from available facts or leave only affected
    knowledge uncertain. Preserve foreign-context/generation safety, explicit capability discovery
    outside callbacks and native-error preservation. Do not hide routine initialization behind repeated
    caught exceptions or introduce a second context/capability service.
  ☑ Migrate complete observation families with generator declarations, cache effects, callers and tests
    together. Remove superseded handwritten plumbing in the same unit; retain complex metadata/dependency
    reconciliation in its existing domain owner. Keep generated native dispatch, OpenGLDriverCalls,
    OpenGLNativeSlot lifetime rooting and loader/uninstall ownership unless a concrete defect requires
    a correction. No preparation hooks, observation receipts, call counters, compatibility shims or
    parallel old/new observers may be introduced.
  ☑ Run delegated canonical Debug/ordinary Release builds, generator diagnostics/compilation tests and
    native boundary regressions after the bulk migration. Cover both GL roots and shared aliases;
    accepted/rejected/uncertain effects; forward-compatible rejected wide lines and supported ordinary
    widths; unchanged native errors; observer faults with targeted recovery; no-capability startup;
    capability-independent publication; context replacement/retirement; and exactly-once native dispatch.
    Assert ordinary unsigned/numeric writes and irrelevant locations preserve active metadata operations,
    availability and revisions without avoidable reads, while represented reentrant changes interrupt
    stale completion. Retain native-state and suppression oracles; no benchmark or timing gate.
  ☑ Reconcile proposal/contracts, source inventory/API coverage, migration receipts and current-state
    documentation. Perform second source review and an independent audit-stage-completion audit before
    checking completion. Keep 8i's separate lifecycle/query-policy redesign and later integration gates open.
  ☑ Completion: handwritten simple observers contain their domain effect logic, generated delivery owns
    shared safety plumbing, proven rejections preserve known facts, irrelevant calls do not disturb
    metadata work, and ordinary context/capability absence uses explicit nonthrowing control flow.

  Qualification: canonical Debug/ordinary Release builds passed; 666/666 focused native tests and
    26/26 generator tests passed in each configuration, with zero skipped tests. Second source review
    and independent completion audit passed. See Rendering.GpuCommands.Migrations.md and local
    artifacts/phase8h.1 closure receipts. No staging or commit; 8i and later gates remain open.

Phase 8i: Redesign metadata tracking around intercepted creation and observed resource changes
  Depends on 8h's native dispatch boundary and 8h.1's corrected classification, relevance ordering
    and simplified query-free observation delivery.
  Authority: the approved RHI ownership/no-shim contracts and the requirement to maintain metadata
    from the complete observed resource lifecycle rather than treating missing tracking as a query trigger.
  Outcome: creation, guaranteed defaults and intercepted configuration maintain canonical manager-owned
    metadata for covered resources; native reads have explicit, limited reasons and consumers reuse known facts.

  ☐ Design and document the complete metadata lifecycle before implementing the redesign. Define resource
    identity, reserved versus realized names, guaranteed defaults, known/unavailable facts, mutation,
    replacement, deletion/name reuse and context/share-group ownership. Review the design against actual
    readers and consumers; identify which metadata is supplied, defaulted, derived or genuinely driver-produced.
    Agree the design before migrating families; retain one canonical manager authority and one cache authority.
  ☐ Build an explicit creation/configuration/deletion coverage inventory from compiler-referenced OpenTK
    bindings and existing RHI operations. Name every supported factory and relevant alias, including
    glGen*/glCreate*, glCreateShader/glCreateShaderProgramv/glCreateProgram, glFenceSync and extension
    allocation/import entrypoints which create or establish native identities. Cover both GL roots and
    supported Core/Ext/Arb entrypoints; preserve existing vendor-owner and legacy-feature exclusions.
    Specify generated names versus realized objects and the later operation that establishes their type.
    Interception coverage gaps are defects to fix, not justification for routine discovery queries.
  ☐ Add generated post-call creation observers and manager registration/default initialization. Consume
    returned names, arrays and native results synchronously with their exact ABI. Never register zero,
    failed results or an unrelated prior allocation under a reused name. Coordinate creation observation
    with backend-owned saved-original dispatch so RHI factories register/publish once rather than twice.
  ☐ Redesign buffer tracking for GpuBufferObject and its role wrappers using GpuBufferMetadata. Maintain
    known size, usage, storage mode/flags and relevant mapping facts from creation/defaults and observed
    allocation/configuration calls. Replace ObserveBufferStorage's blanket withdrawal where supplied
    arguments establish represented facts; preserve storage identity and dependent buffer-texture lifetimes.
  ☐ Redesign texture/image tracking for GpuTexture, BorrowedTexture, GpuTextureView, GpuBufferTexture,
    GpuBufferView and renderbuffer-backed texture associations using GpuTextureMetadata and GpuImageMetadata.
    Carry target, dimensions, format, levels/layers, storage mode, represented parameters, view ranges and
    backing associations from observed commands. Fix observers such as ObserveTextureStorage2D that
    currently discard supplied dimensions/format/mip counts. Separate content-only writes from descriptor
    changes; retain source-storage identities and image projections without a second metadata mirror.
  ☐ Redesign renderbuffer, framebuffer and sampler tracking using GpuRenderbufferMetadata,
    GpuFramebufferMetadata and GpuSamplerMetadata. Maintain storage, attachments/subresources, routing,
    attachmentless defaults and represented sampler parameters from observed lifecycle/configuration calls.
    Include bound, named and multi-bind effects where applicable, plus attachment/dependency retirement.
  ☐ Redesign shader/program/pipeline tracking for GpuShaderModule, GpuProgramObject, GpuProgramLayout and
    GpuProgramPipeline using GpuShaderMetadata, GpuProgramMetadata and GpuProgramPipelineMetadata.
    Maintain declared stages, configuration, selection and known interface assignments from observed calls.
    Treat compilation/link status and executable reflection as specifically identified driver-produced
    results; do not reflect an entire interface after an ordinary represented assignment.
  ☐ Cover GpuVao, GpuTransformFeedback, GpuQuery, GpuSync, GpuSemaphore and GpuMemoryObject using
    GpuVertexArrayMetadata, GpuTransformFeedbackMetadata, GpuQueryMetadata, GpuSyncMetadata,
    GpuSemaphoreMetadata and GpuMemoryObjectMetadata. Register observed creation/defaults and track
    represented configuration/lifetime facts. Keep execution-owned binding/activity knowledge in its
    existing cache domain; do not invent canonical fields or layout mirrors solely to avoid an empty schema.
  ☐ Define accepted/rejected/uncertain native outcome policy for each operation family. External calls
    execute once unchanged and observers never veto them or leak errors. Retain known state after proven
    rejection; use supplied requests for ordinary tracked properties under the approved metadata policy.
    Do not equate a void native return with proven success, consume GL errors or add universal verification
    reads, per-call GL.Is* checks, requested/actual mirrors or a new generic transaction framework.
    Specify any unresolved outcome requiring a targeted read and its concrete consumer need.
  ☐ Restrict acquisition to explicit cases: resources predating installation, supported external imports
    whose descriptors cannot be obtained from their intercepted setup, identified driver-produced results,
    or documented unresolved outcomes. Keep approved sample-count resolution/fallback policy explicit.
    Unknown registration or a discarded command argument alone must not trigger a query. Distinguish an
    interception/tracking defect from genuinely unavailable input; fix the producer rather than silently
    recapturing metadata on ordinary reads, binding, validation or reference conversion.
  ☐ Audit every metadata reader, acquisition/recovery entry point and its consumers against the new
    lifecycle. Remove obsolete readback/invalidation paths and update initialization, adoption, aliases,
    dependencies and context-local tools together. Review interruption guards against real production
    acquisition/publication callbacks; keep only protections required by those remaining operations,
    with scoped cleanup and targeted uncertainty. Preserve 8h.1's relevance-before-interruption ordering
    when introducing creation/default/configuration tracking. Synthetic reentry tests alone do not justify machinery.
  ☐ Migrate each complete operation family atomically: creation/default publication, observed mutations,
    readers, consumers, failure/deletion handling and tests. Remove superseded APIs in that unit; introduce
    no compatibility shims, parallel registry, second publication route or generic event/command bus.
    Backend-specific interpretation stays beneath RHI; wrappers and portable APIs receive semantic facts.
  ☐ Qualify with delegated canonical Debug/ordinary Release builds and focused lifecycle regressions.
    Verify creation → configuration → consumption with descriptor readers configured to reject unexpected
    reads; cover engine/raw OpenTK resources and RHI-owned resources, aliases/views, delayed realization,
    external imports, name reuse, failed/invalid commands, context recreation and initial adoption.
    Assert exactly-once registration/publication/native dispatch, stable suppression and no redundant
    descriptor reads; independently test legitimate driver-produced results and approved narrow fallbacks.
    Update obsolete managed-wrapper capture fixtures to the actual native boundary where necessary.
    No benchmark, timing study, instrumented Release, game launch or automatic commit is required.
  ☐ Reconcile the approved design, RHI contracts, resource inventory/API coverage, metadata acquisition
    analysis and permanent ownership documentation. Perform second review and independent completion audit
    for coverage and data flow, not just symbol presence. Keep remaining native-hook qualification explicit.
  ☐ Completion: every covered resource has an observed identity/default/configuration lifecycle; ordinary
    metadata consumers reuse maintained canonical facts, and every remaining query has an explicit reason
    supported by an actual consumer. No missing observation is disguised as normal acquisition/recovery.

Phase 8j: Qualify corrective closure and reconcile documentation
  Depends on 8a–8i, including 8h.1.

  ☐ Record before/after routes for every named audit finding and any additional helper-chain occurrence.
    Review actual dependency direction as well as native execution location; demonstrate one admitted
    RHI entry route and existing manager/cache authority for each affected operation family.
  ☐ Expand RHIContractIsolationTests beyond direct method signatures and the image/framebuffer schema
    list: inspect reachable project-owned payload fields/properties in RHICommandContext and
    IRHIResourceExecution contracts, including buffer, shader, program/reflection and initialization
    schemas. Detect nested OpenTK types, native reflection property bags and native-token interpretation
    above the backend; cover semantic enum conversion/codec boundaries with focused checks and caller review.
    Avoid treating a clean signature scan as proof that transitive payloads or consumers are backend-neutral.
  ☐ Explicitly qualify intentional boundaries: RHICommandContext.Composition selects the concrete backend
    only at its thin composition root; RHIShaderBinary.NativeFormat remains a private opaque executable-cache
    payload with cache policy above the backend. Native adoption identities/platform external handles and
    backend/interception adapters remain confined to their explicit integration contracts. Verify none leaks
    native selectors/types into portable consumer APIs; add no redundant facade or duplicate owner to hide them.
  ☐ Run delegated Debug/Release builds and focused behavior regressions on the combined candidate for
    admission, creation failure, acquisition/recovery, dependency publication, labels, suppression,
    context-local tools, retirement and immediate/recorded equivalence. Keep inherited failures explicit;
    integrated lighting/package/user acceptance stays in Phase 9, with no repeated benchmark requirement.
  ☐ Complete second review and independent stage-completion audit against the proposal, contracts,
    every named correction and mandatory migration receipts. Resolve gaps before claiming closure;
    reflection inventories or namespace-only searches do not substitute for caller/dependency review.
  ☐ Reconcile proposal/contracts, migration receipts, inventory/coverage, parent-plan cross-references,
    Rendering.GpuResources.md and Rendering.ShaderBindingState.md with final ownership and actual routes.
    Permanent documentation describes implemented behavior; historical receipts retain their limitations.
  ☐ Completion: all correction units and their caller dependencies satisfy the final RHI boundary with
    retained manager lifetimes, no alternate owner-side execution/acquisition route and no temporary shim.

Phase 8k: Align resource-management service names with RHI ownership
  Depends on 8j; final corrective subphase before integrated qualification.

  ☐ Inventory Gpu-prefixed management, registration and lifecycle services by responsibility. Establish
    an explicit old/new name map, including GpuResourceManager → RHIResourceManager,
    GpuResourceManagerSystem → RHIResourceManagerSystem and GpuResourceDisposalQueue → RHIResourceDisposalQueue.
    Review GpuBindingRegistry, GpuUniformRingSystem and GpuUniformRingFrameController for RHI service
    naming according to their final ownership; do not mechanically rename every Gpu-prefixed type.
    Resource wrappers, canonical metadata and consumer references retain their existing names/contracts.
  ☐ Apply the management-service rename in one coherent sweep across all partial declarations, filenames,
    production and test callers, composition/lifecycle hooks, generated-code inputs and relevant tooling.
    Preserve native execution, initialization/publication authority, context identity, cleanup ordering
    and API behavior. This is a naming correction, not a resource-model or ownership redesign.
  ☐ Update proposal/contracts, inventory/coverage, parent-plan cross-references and permanent architecture
    documentation to match the final names. Keep historical receipts intelligible without rewriting their
    original evidence. Remove superseded names from active APIs/callers; introduce no compatibility alias,
    forwarding class, duplicate service or staged migration shim.
  ☐ Run delegated canonical Debug/ordinary Release builds and focused initialization, registration,
    disposal, context-lifetime and binding regressions after the complete rename. Perform second review
    and independent completion audit, checking symbol/file consistency and unchanged dependency direction.
    No benchmark, timing study, instrumented Release or automatic commit is required or authorized.
  ☐ Completion: management services consistently use uppercase RHI names where their responsibility
    belongs to the RHI, all callers/documentation agree, and retained resource contracts remain unchanged.

Phase 9: Qualify integrated behavior and release artifacts
  Depends on Phase 8, including subphases 8a–8k and 8h.1.
  Outcome: correctness, package identity and outstanding live evidence are explicit.

  ☐ Run delegated focused and integrated regressions on an immutable candidate, covering all family receipts,
    original-context retirement, aliases/views, local tools, context loss, rejected commands, exactly-once
    external calls and immediate/recorded equivalence. Keep hardware coverage gaps explicit.
    Correct inherited integration fixtures identified against pre-interception HEAD 9de4c4ca:
    ShaderTextureTargetTests must verify semantic conversion rather than native enum numeric equality;
    AmbientOcclusionCompositeTests must supply the complete retained resource table required by the RHI.
    Preserve their independent output assertions; these baseline failures are not waived by focused
    native-interception qualification. Reconcile all 477 baseline-proven failures in
    artifacts/phase8h/closure5-head-comparison.json, including mock setup, complete shader resource
    tables and vertex/target declarations. Diagnose the fourteen full-sequence unmatched observations
    (exposure, particle capture/handback, installed depth, sampler/worker cleanup and local exposure)
    with equivalent workload ordering; they pass the final 662-case combined selection but that does
    not certify their earlier full-suite sequence or attribute its cause. Preserve numerical oracles
    and tolerances, and resolve any actual runtime defect before integrated acceptance.
    Investigate PbrLumOnFullPipelineIntegrationTests' direct-only composite numerical mismatch after
    correcting its depth-comparison inputs and complete MRT declaration. Preserve the independent oracle
    and existing tolerance; do not treat source-boundary qualification as integrated lighting acceptance.
  ☐ Run canonical Debug/Release build and package tooling through subagents; verify installed/package
    identity where the repository workflow requires it. Confirm diagnostic counters remain DEBUG-only.
    Do not create an instrumented Release product.
  ☐ Review storage reuse and allocation sites; verify immediate calls need no recording allocation and
    recording requires no per-command heap object. Use focused behavioral checks for stable binding
    suppression and reuse of available metadata without redundant queries. No timing thresholds or
    before/after benchmark comparison are required for completion.
  ☐ Provide a user-run visual/runtime checklist for graphics, compute, cloud/depth content ordering,
    resize, shader reload and teardown. Record actual user evidence separately from headless tests;
    leave live appearance/runtime-behavior acceptance unchecked until supplied.
  ☐ Reconcile every proposal requirement with implementation and evidence; resolve deviations or obtain
    explicit scope approval rather than declaring unimplemented requirements complete.
  ☐ Completion: all required correctness/package receipts and user-run acceptance are recorded;
    remaining unsupported hardware evidence is disclosed, and no unapproved architecture deviation remains.

Final acceptance
  ☐ All nine phases, their subphases and mandatory migration receipts are satisfied; later cleanup never substitutes for
    removing superseded APIs within their owning migration unit.
  ☐ Final APIs are backend-neutral, managed OpenGL execution requires 4.5, and every native operation has
    one execution owner with existing manager metadata/lifetime authority and preserved cache behavior.
  ☐ GraphicsCommandContext and StateCache's old execution/name surfaces are gone; shader/PSO, geometry,
    targets, uniforms, synchronization and recording follow the approved final contracts.
  ☐ Tests, current-state docs, package verification and user-run evidence support the claimed outcome
    without performance claims or treating headless results as visual acceptance.

Proposal coverage map
  Boundary, operations, capabilities and resource inputs: Phases 1–5; final cache split in Phase 7.
  Creation/adoption, initial content, original identity and retirement: Phases 2–5; corrections in 8; lifecycle tests in 6/9.
  Shader/PSO creation, generation identity, replacement and ownership: Phase 5; recorded rejection in 6.
  Geometry, attachment targets and immediate submission: Phase 5; recorded consumption in 6.
  Uniform capture, physical publication and history: Phase 5; recording/epoch/cancellation tests in 6.
  Recording, ownership transfer, tickets, failure and CPU/GPU completion: Phases 4/6.
  Dependency inversion for manager services, wrappers and semantic RHI objects: subphases 5b–5e and 8a–8j.
  Semantic buffer/shader/reflection schemas and authored resource types: subphase 8d.
  Manager operation guards, context discovery and backend-only boundary footprints: subphase 8f.
  Transitive schema isolation and intentional composition/native-payload boundary qualification: subphase 8j.
  Persistent state knowledge and removal of obsolete frame/resize/startup purges: subphase 8g.
  Native OpenTK dispatch, observational forwarding and remaining handler propagation: subphase 8h.
  Observer classification, generated safety plumbing, effect relevance and nonthrowing startup: subphase 8h.1.
  Complete creation interception and maintained lifecycle metadata with bounded acquisition: subphase 8i.
  RHI management-service naming and complete caller/documentation reconciliation: subphase 8k.
  Native dispatch, publication, exact integration and no-shim migration: mandatory receipts, Phases 2–8.
  Representative outcomes, efficient-execution checks, package and user-run qualification: Phase 9, supported
    by focused verification and current-state documentation in every owning migration unit.
